    "reviewed_content": [
      "Reviewed the 10 blessing pages and item/weapon associations in the fixed 88-file scope; the four implementations cover eight bindings: Atrox tactical axe Mk II/IV/VII, Maccabian duelling sword Mk II/IV/V, Branx Mk III Arbites shock maul, and Chirurgeon Mk IV bone saw.",
      "The four own tier tables consistently provide melee_power_level_modifier .04/.06/.08/.10 and a two-second child duration. Parent/child offset -1 leaves five effective layers; formatter and the four reconstructed RAW tier strings agree on +4/+6/+8/+10%, two seconds, and five stacks.",
      "The actual parent checks held slot, exact source item and on_hit with the same-target helper. The first qualifying hit on a different target records that target and clears prior layers without updating last_hit_time; subsequent hits on that target add one layer and refresh the shared timer. At cap, another qualifying same-target event refreshes; expiry removes child stacks on a later parent update.",
      "Attack damage is calculated before stagger/on_hit event handling, and the new layer contributes only after the later stat-cache update. The melee power modifier enters the melee Power pool; both examples state normalized post-curve inputs and do not promise equal final health damage.",
      "Actual routing differences are represented: bound ordinary/light/heavy/sweep and push profiles use their real per-Mark routes; pure push may advance the hit tracker but does not consume melee_power_level_modifier. Branx Mk III special is a direct melee sweep with a separate stun primer and no imported explosion. Chirurgeon Mk IV initial sticky hit is an ordinary melee event; both delayed rip profiles use current melee power but skip on-hit proc, so they do not add or refresh stacks. Mode setup and saw coating toggle are not hit events.",
      "Switching away suppresses held-gated contribution and new source-item procs while the existing timer continues; switching back before expiry can restore remaining stacks. True removal destroys the parent and its externally controlled child stacks. The RAW comparison classifies omitted held/item/special/push details as not covered, not as contradictions.",
      "The verified image receipt points to actual icon weapon_trait_183, 128x128, matching public hash and attachment. Own reverse links and the eight-item map/binding associations are present in the fixed scope."
    ],
